  "sport": "soccer",
  "title": "Meet in the middle – feint past",
  "description": "Two lines face each other about 10 metres apart, and the first player in each line has a ball. Both dribble towards each other at the same time, make a feint when they meet in the middle and dribble past. Then hand the ball over to the first player in the other line and join the back of it.\n\nStart with just dribbling and passing across as a warm-up. Then add feints: a pass fake, a shot fake and a step-over. Progression: put a defender in the middle. With lots of players, run several lanes side by side. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Look up – switch your eyes between the ball and what is around you."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Lots of touches, ball close to the body. Dribble with the outside of the foot."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Pass fake: look at a teammate, start the passing movement and stop before you hit the ball."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Step-over: step over the ball one way, shift your weight and take the ball the other way."
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en",
  "phase": "warmup",
  "difficulty": 1,
